  Early wizards desperately need to forget spell casting.  Later, (much
MUCH later) they'll be unstoppable spell casting machines.  At the start
of the game they are death on two legs.  Their OWN death.  

  Until you get your AC below 0 wear the best armor that doesn't make
you burdened.  (Early non-cursed crystal plate mail will break your
heart.)  After that keep improving until you can wear (studded) leather
armor and still have AC below 0.  (Below 0 your AC starts reducing
damage taken.)  Be sure to check the armor left by leather golems.  I
found +4 once.  

  NB: Studded leather only gives one more point of AC than leather armor
and weighs more.  So always wear (plain) leather if it has a higher
enchantment than studded.

  Especially check accessory armor: helmets, boots, shields, gloves.
You'll see a lot more of these so they're more likely to have a high
enchantment.  A single +4 enchantment can break the early game wide
open.

  Once you switch to leather body armor you're golden for casting
spells.  Only one out of the seven spell schools is attack.  For the
rest you can remove accessory armor as necessary when not in combat.

  This is the most important discovery I made about spell casting.  It
makes spell casting practical much earlier.

  Shields and helmets especially.  They only take one turn to take off
or put on.  #adjust them to 'T' and 'W' respectively.  'TTTW' will
remove them both.  'WWWT' will wear them both.  Gloves also only take
one turn to remove/wear, but only Gauntlets of Power interfere with
spell casting. 

  Better yet, with leather armor generally it's just the shield that
keeps spell casting failure rates above 50%.  Since it's just one turn
to put on a shield you can 'Z'ap force bolt until the monster is one
turn away, then wear the shield.  If you have magic missile this works
even better.

  Get daggers and throw daggers.  #Enhance to Expert ASAP.  Then wield
your best non-cursed dagger and dump the quarterstaff.  That lets you
wear the best shield you can find.  (I found a +4 elven shield once.  I
wore it.)  Expert thrown daggers do double damage.  

  If you find Gauntlets of Power that's +6 damage bonus, doubled to +12.
It's also out to range Str/2.  Throw early and often.  Hitting monsters
that can't hit you back is the definition of bliss in NetHack.

  Looks like a lot of trouble, right?  Well, it is.  But if you want to
grow up to be a Real Wizard with 1000 mana points, all spells, and the
Eye of Aethiopica, that's how to do it.  Do that a few times and you'll
realize how puny an early wizard's spell casting powers really are.



